course: dictionary
lesson: 6040
title: Member: someone who belongs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A member is a person who belongs to a group, like a club, a team or a family. «Pets are family members for many people» shows that a family member can even be a pet, because it belongs to the family.
explain: Look at the words around member to find its meaning. «If you get lost in a shop, go to a till and tell a staff member.» A staff member works there, so they can help you. The clue is the word staff, which tells you the person works in the shop.
explain: A member can also be a thing in a set. In maths, 2 is a member of the set of even numbers, because 2 belongs in that group of numbers.
fact: A member is a person who belongs to a group, such as a club, a team or a family.
fact: «Members» are the people in a group: a club has members, and so does a team.
fact: A member can also be an animal or thing that belongs to a group or set.
fact: A lion is a member of the cat family.
fact: «Member of Parliament» means someone who is elected to speak for people in a country's parliament.
exercise: «Sadness about a pet is real, because pets are family members for many people.» What is a family member? | *A person or pet who belongs to a family | A room in the house where people eat | A bird that lives in a tree | A kind of food
exercise: «If you get lost in a shop, tell a staff member.» Who is a staff member? | A person who sells only sweets | A child with a shopping bag | *Someone who works at the shop and can help you | A shopper who is lost too
exercise: In maths, which number is a member of the set of even numbers? | 7 | *2 | 5 | 3
test: What word means a person who belongs to a club or team? | Visitor | *Member | Stranger | Guest
test: In science, a lion is a member of which family? | *The cat family | Fish | Trees | Birds
exam: In «The Grammy Awards are voted on by members of the Recording Academy, people who work in music, not by fans», who are the members? | Songs played on the radio | *People who belong to the Recording Academy and work in music | Gold awards on a shelf | Fans who buy tickets
